From 93f2fb1f333f999d209dad0debab56731db99b98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab <homelab@emrys.dev>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:56:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] api: scope every snapshot endpoint, attribute to the
 token's owner

The API's owner is the API token's owner: django-ninja resolves the bearer
token to APIToken.created_by, so the crawl created by POST /core/snapshots
carries that user and the snapshot is stamped from it. A crawl id belonging
to someone else is 404, and reuse-by-URL is per owner.

List, detail, RSS, archive results, crawls, tag exports and the legacy
/api/v1/cli/* commands are all filtered by the same scope, so no filter,
search or id can reach another user's capture.
